{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/stronglyconnectedcomponents()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stronglyConnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV","text":"Components","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Components are in the order Tarjan’s algorithm completes them, on a depth-first search","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with roots in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order and successors in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"text":" order. That is a reverse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"topological order of the condensation: every edge between components goes from a later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component to an earlier one, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed()"},{"text":" lists the components with every edge going","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"forward. Each component lists its vertices in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so on a graph whose vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions are insertion order ("},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), one sort by that vertex’s position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"puts the components in insertion order, O(C log C) for C components:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.stronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On any graph, one pass over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, O(V):"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let components = graph.stronglyConnectedComponents()","let inVertexOrder = graph.vertices.compactMap { vertex in","    let component = components[components.component(of: vertex)]","    return component.first == vertex ? component : nil","}"]},{"name":"Complexity","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(V + E)."}]}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/stronglyConnectedComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The strongly connected components: maximal sets of vertices each reaching every other, by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Tarjan’s algorithm."}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typ